748090c4daec3d534096aa505", "bytes": 164000, "lines": 379, "events_no_deltas": [{"type": "system", "subtype": "init", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "tools": ["StructuredOutput"], "mcp_servers": [], "permissionMode": "auto", "claude_code_version": "2.1.294", "output_style": "default", "init_sha256": "19a6ffcf0781096cd8fadcc901d1f698c81748761870f4f438dc6f07a56b3d9a"}, {"type": "system", "subtype": "status", "status": "requesting"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "message_start", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgAqwTiKjwhRbyUvjdH3L", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 354, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5698, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 354}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "ttft_ms": 4323, "thinking_display": "updates"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 0, "content_block": {"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "thinking_display": "updates"}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgAqwTiKjwhRbyUvjdH3L", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": {"длина": 30644, "sha256": "afddf41e88a56e320ac0fa06366a65afee60e3661c899abb07724718cf1deecb"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 354, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5698, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 354}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T02:58:58.125Z", "request_id": "req_011CgAqwTPyGh7JfCSzLuMQu", "thinking_duration_ms": 113820}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 0}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 1, "content_block": {"type": "text", "text": ""}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgAqwTiKjwhRbyUvjdH3L", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I pick **candidate 7**. It has the highest expected profit of the eight plans. I traced each plan by hand on average demand (forecast × 1.046), rounded, with no code run.\n\n**What decides it**\n\n- **Order frequency.** Each day with an order costs a fixed 52.\n  - Candidates 5 and 6 order every 2 days, 14 times in total (728 in fees). That is about 260 more than the 3-day plans pay, and the extra orders buy almost nothing back.\n  - Candidates 0, 3 and 4 order every 4 days (8 orders). A batch of item 1 then has to last all 4 days of its shelf life. Any surplus goes straight to write-off and there is no buffer.\n  - Candidates 1, 2 and 7 order every 3 days (9 orders). A batch of item 1 covers 3 days, and any leftover sells on its 4th day. That spare day softens shortages and write-offs when demand swings. This gain is larger than the 52 saved by dropping one order.\n- **Warehouse limit (136).**\n  - Candidate 0 overflows: on day 5 (48 + 100 = 148) and day 9 (61 + 96 = 157).\n  - Candidate 3 builds up stock of item 0 (it orders about 1.1× forecast), so it runs out of space on days 21 and 25 (about 145–147). It loses some of item 1, which it already orders thin.\n  - Candidate 4 has no space problems. But it orders exactly the forecast, about 4–5% below average demand, so it regularly pays shortage penalties.\n- **Comparing the 3-day plans.**\n  - Candidate 2 orders exactly the forecast, below average demand. With a penalty of 12 per missing unit (lost margin plus fine), it comes up short too often.\n  - Candidate 1 orders about 1.2× forecast. That is more item 0 than gets sold (about 549 against about 478 expected demand), plus extra write-offs of item 1 and overflow risk.\n  - Candidate 7 orders about 1.1× forecast for item 0 and about 1.14× forecast (about 1.09× average) for item 1. That matches a cost-balanced order level here (the critical ratio is about 0.7).\n\n**Candidate 7's own losses.** It overflows on day 14, losing about 11 units of item 1 out of 118. That batch was ordered with extra room anyway, so it costs about 55. Day 26 is close to the limit. It ends with about 25 units of item 0 left over. Under random demand it is still the most stable plan, because of the spare shelf day for item 1 and the stock buffer for item 0."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 354, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5698, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 354}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T02:59:06.872Z", "request_id": "req_011CgAqwTPyGh7JfCSzLuMQu"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_015gYWdeDpiFcr9JFpycxvxr", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgAqwTiKjwhRbyUvjdH3L", "typ